CORE broken-smt-backend
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ char16_t: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ wchar_t: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
pointer outside object bounds.*: FAILURE$
--
N5008 [lex.string]/9 (C11 6.4.5/6 likewise): a string literal object has
static storage duration, so `const char16_t *p = u"ab"' points to its
first element and p[0..2] are within it.  A wide string literal is an
array constant, and the bit-vector encoding of object_size gave no size
to objects other than symbols and narrow string constants: every access
failed "pointer outside object bounds" (bin53, also in C).  Array
constants now have the size of their type.  The SMT backend fails an
invariant on the address of an array constant (smt2_conv.cpp,
convert_address_of_rec, bin53 too).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
